('Beatitudes · "cleanses us, completes us and radiates"',191,
 'This is the "be perfect, as your heavenly Father is perfect" of Matthew 5:48 (Chapter 10), now given flesh: not flawless performance, but a heart so conformed to Christ that His own blessedness - His own love - radiates through us.',
 'This is the call to be perfect as our heavenly Father is perfect (cf. Matthew 5:48; Chapter 10, on communion), now given flesh: not a flawless record, but a heart so conformed to Christ that His own blessedness—His own love—cleanses us, completes us and radiates through us.'),
